# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Function sizes {#function-sizes}"
msgstr "Mga laki ng function {#function-sizes}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Every job runs at one size: `S`, `M`, or `L`. If the size is too small, the job is rejected. If it is larger than needed, the job runs on a bigger compute profile than the work requires. See [Function sizes](/guides/managed-workflow-compute-profiles#best-practice-match-sizes-to-problem-sizes) for how sizes work in general.\n"
msgstr "Bawat job ay tumatakbo sa isang laki: `S`, `M`, o `L`. Kung masyadong maliit ang laki, ire-reject ang job. Kung mas malaki ito kaysa sa kailangan, tatakbo ang job sa mas malaking compute profile kaysa sa hinihingi ng trabaho. Tingnan ang [Function sizes](/guides/managed-workflow-compute-profiles#best-practice-match-sizes-to-problem-sizes) para sa kung paano gumagana ang mga laki sa pangkalahatan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Pass the size to `solver.run()` with the `function_size` argument. For the Optimization Solver, the size depends on the number of binary decision variables and the interaction density of the problem.\n"
msgstr "Ipasa ang laki sa `solver.run()` gamit ang argument na `function_size`. Para sa Optimization Solver, nakadepende ang laki sa bilang ng binary decision variable at sa interaction density ng problema.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Interaction density is the fraction of possible variable pairs that appear together in at least one term of the objective function or constraints. Each distinct pair is counted once. For sizing, equality constraints contribute interactions between every pair of variables they contain. Continue to pass hard constraints directly through the `constraint` input, as shown in the constrained optimization example.\n"
msgstr "Ang interaction density ay ang bahagi ng mga posibleng pares ng variable na magkasamang lumalabas sa kahit isang term ng objective function o ng mga constraint. Bawat natatanging pares ay binibilang nang isang beses. Para sa sizing, ang mga equality constraint ay nag-aambag ng mga interaksyon sa pagitan ng bawat pares ng variable na nilalaman nila. Patuloy na ipasa ang mga hard constraint nang direkta sa pamamagitan ng input na `constraint`, gaya ng ipinapakita sa constrained optimization example.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Size | Binary decision variables | Interaction density | Rule |\n"
"| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n"
"| `S` | ≤ 50 | ≤ 10% | Both metrics must satisfy the Small limits. |\n"
"| `M` | ≤ 100 | ≤ 25% | At least one metric exceeds its Small limit, but both remain within the Medium limits. |\n"
"| `L` | > 100 | > 25% | Either the variable count or interaction density exceeds its Medium limit. |\n"
msgstr ""
"| Laki | Mga binary decision variable | Interaction density | Patakaran |\n"
"| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n"
"| `S` | ≤ 50 | ≤ 10% | Dapat pasok ang parehong sukatan sa mga limitasyon ng Small. |\n"
"| `M` | ≤ 100 | ≤ 25% | Lampas sa limitasyon ng Small ang kahit isang sukatan, pero pasok pa rin ang dalawa sa mga limitasyon ng Medium. |\n"
"| `L` | > 100 | > 25% | Lampas sa limitasyon ng Medium ang bilang ng variable o ang interaction density. |\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Both the variable count and the interaction density must satisfy the selected size. For example, a problem with 40 variables and 30% interaction density requires `\"L\"`.\n"
msgstr "Dapat pasok sa napiling laki ang parehong bilang ng variable at interaction density. Halimbawa, ang problemang may 40 variable at 30% interaction density ay nangangailangan ng `\"L\"`.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For graph problems, count the binary decision variables in the optimization model. Depending on the formulation, a single graph node can require more than one variable.\n"
msgstr "Para sa mga graph problem, bilangin ang mga binary decision variable sa optimization model. Depende sa formulation, ang isang graph node ay maaaring mangailangan ng higit sa isang variable.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Calculate the size before submitting {#calculate-the-size-before-submitting}"
msgstr "Kalkulahin ang laki bago mag-submit {#calculate-the-size-before-submitting}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Use the following helper to calculate the size from the number of binary decision variables and the number of distinct interacting variable pairs, including the pairs that hard constraints introduce. It returns `\"S\"`, `\"M\"`, or `\"L\"`, and no job is submitted. The examples that follow show how to count the variables and pairs for a graph problem and for a constrained problem.\n"
msgstr "Gamitin ang sumusunod na helper para kalkulahin ang laki mula sa bilang ng binary decision variable at ng bilang ng natatanging magkakaugnay na pares ng variable, kasama ang mga pares na idinudulot ng mga hard constraint. Ibinabalik nito ang `\"S\"`, `\"M\"`, o `\"L\"`, at walang job na isa-submit. Ipinapakita ng mga sumusunod na halimbawa kung paano bilangin ang mga variable at pares para sa isang graph problem at para sa isang constrained na problema.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "If the size is too small, the job fails with error `4600`, and the message names the size to use instead. If it is larger than needed, the job runs normally and records a `4601` advisory event. See [Function sizes](/guides/managed-workflow-compute-profiles#best-practice-match-sizes-to-problem-sizes) to learn more.\n"
msgstr "Kung masyadong maliit ang laki, mabibigo ang job na may error na `4600`, at ipapangalan ng mensahe ang laki na dapat gamitin. Kung mas malaki ito kaysa sa kailangan, normal na tatakbo ang job at magtatala ng `4601` advisory event. Tingnan ang [Function sizes](/guides/managed-workflow-compute-profiles#best-practice-match-sizes-to-problem-sizes) para matuto pa.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Example: Unconstrained optimization {#example-unconstrained-optimization}"
msgstr "Halimbawa: Unconstrained na optimization {#example-unconstrained-optimization}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Run the [maximum cut](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Maximum_cut) (max-cut) problem. The following example demonstrates the Solver's capabilities on a 100-node, 3-regular unweighted graph max-cut problem, but you can also solve weighted graph problems.\n"
"In addition to `qiskit-ibm-catalog`, you will also use the following packages to run this example: `networkx` and `numpy`. You can install these packages by uncommenting the following cell if you are running this example in a notebook using the IPython kernel.\n"
msgstr ""
"Patakbuhin ang [maximum cut](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Maximum_cut) (Max-Cut) na problema. Ipinapakita ng sumusunod na halimbawa ang kakayahan ng Solver sa isang 100-node, 3-regular na unweighted graph Max-Cut problem, ngunit maaari ka ring lumutas ng mga weighted graph problem.\n"
"Bukod sa `qiskit-ibm-catalog`, gagamitin mo rin ang mga sumusunod na package para patakbuhin ang halimbawang ito: `networkx` at `numpy`. Maaari mong i-install ang mga package na ito sa pamamagitan ng pag-uncomment ng sumusunod na cell kung pinapatakbo mo ang halimbawang ito sa isang notebook gamit ang IPython kernel.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "1. Define the problem {#1-define-the-problem}"
msgstr "1. Tukuyin ang problema {#1-define-the-problem}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "You can run a max-cut problem by defining a graph problem and specifying `problem_type='maxcut'`.\n"
msgstr "Maaari kang magpatakbo ng Max-Cut problem sa pamamagitan ng pagde-define ng graph problem at pagtukoy ng `problem_type='maxcut'`.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/guides/q-ctrl-optimization-solver/extracted-outputs/0a7255e1-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/guides/q-ctrl-optimization-solver/extracted-outputs/0a7255e1-0.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The Solver accepts a string as the problem definition input.\n"
msgstr "Tumatanggap ang Solver ng string bilang input ng depinisyon ng problema.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "2. Run the problem {#2-run-the-problem}"
msgstr "2. Patakbuhin ang problema {#2-run-the-problem}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "When using the graph-based input method, specify the problem type. Calculate the function size from `maxcut_graph`, then pass the returned value to `solver.run` through `function_size`.\n"
msgstr "Kapag gumagamit ng graph-based na paraan ng input, tukuyin ang uri ng problema. Kalkulahin ang function size mula sa `maxcut_graph`, pagkatapos ay ipasa ang ibinalik na halaga sa `solver.run` sa pamamagitan ng `function_size`.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Check your quantum function workload's [status](/guides/functions-get-started#check-job-status) or return [results](/guides/functions-get-started#retrieve-results) as follows:\n"
msgstr "Suriin ang [status](/guides/functions-get-started#check-job-status) ng iyong quantum function workload o kunin ang [mga resulta](/guides/functions-get-started#retrieve-results) tulad ng sumusunod:\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "3. Retrieve the result {#3-retrieve-the-result}"
msgstr "3. Kunin ang resulta {#3-retrieve-the-result}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Retrieve the optimal cut value from the results dictionary.\n"
msgstr "Kunin ang pinakamainam na halaga ng cut mula sa results dictionary.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"   The mapping of the variables to the bitstring may have changed. The output dictionary contains a `variables_to_bitstring_index_map` sub-dictionary, which helps to verify the ordering.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"   Maaaring nagbago ang pagma-map ng mga variable sa bitstring. Ang output dictionary ay naglalaman ng `variables_to_bitstring_index_map` sub-dictionary, na tumutulong sa pag-verify ng pagkakasunod-sunod.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "You can verify the accuracy of the result by solving the problem classically with open-source solvers like [PuLP](https://coin-or.github.io/pulp/) if the graph is not densely connected. High density problems may require advanced classical solvers to validate the solution.\n"
msgstr "Maaari mong ma-verify ang katumpakan ng resulta sa pamamagitan ng paglutas ng problema nang klasikal gamit ang mga open-source solver tulad ng [PuLP](https://coin-or.github.io/pulp/) kung hindi masyadong siksik ang koneksyon ng graph. Para sa mga problemang may mataas na density, maaaring kailangan ng mas advanced na classical solver para ma-validate ang solusyon.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Example: Constrained optimization {#example-constrained-optimization}"
msgstr "Halimbawa: Constrained na optimization {#example-constrained-optimization}"

# doq: fixed after review 2026-09-29
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The prior max-cut example is a common quadratic unconstrained binary optimization problem. Q-CTRL's Optimization Solver can also solve constrained optimization problems by passing hard constraints directly to the Solver through the `constraint` input, instead of encoding them as penalty terms in the objective function. The Solver currently supports Hamming-weight-1 constraints: each constraint specifies a group of variables where exactly one variable must equal 1 and the rest must equal 0.\n"
msgstr "Ang naunang halimbawa ng max-cut ay isang karaniwang quadratic unconstrained binary optimization problem. Kaya ring lutasin ng Q-CTRL's Optimization Solver ang mga constrained optimization problem sa pamamagitan ng pagpasa ng mga hard constraint nang direkta sa Solver sa pamamagitan ng `constraint` input, imbes na i-encode ang mga ito bilang mga penalty term sa objective function. Kasalukuyang sinusuportahan ng Solver ang mga Hamming-weight-1 constraint: bawat constraint ay tumutukoy ng isang grupo ng mga variable kung saan eksaktong isang variable lang ang dapat maging 1 at ang natitira ay dapat maging 0.\n"

# doq: fixed after review 2026-09-29
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The following example demonstrates how to construct a cost function and a set of hard constraints for a constrained optimization problem, [graph partitioning](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Graph_partition), by assigning every node in a graph to exactly one of several groups while minimizing the total weight of edges whose endpoints land in the same group.\n"
"In addition to the `qiskit-ibm-catalog` and `qiskit` packages, you will also use the following packages to run this example: `numpy`, `networkx`, and `sympy`. You can install these packages by uncommenting the following cell if you are running this example in a notebook using the IPython kernel.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ipinapakita ng sumusunod na halimbawa kung paano bumuo ng cost function at isang set ng mga hard constraint para sa isang constrained optimization problem, [graph partitioning](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Graph_partition), sa pamamagitan ng pagtatalaga ng bawat node sa isang graph sa eksaktong isa sa ilang mga grupo habang mini-minimize ang kabuuang timbang ng mga edge kung saan ang mga endpoint ay napapadpad sa parehong grupo.\n"
"Bukod sa mga package na `qiskit-ibm-catalog` at `qiskit`, gagamitin mo rin ang mga sumusunod na package para patakbuhin ang halimbawang ito: `numpy`, `networkx`, at `sympy`. Maaari mong i-install ang mga package na ito sa pamamagitan ng pag-uncomment ng sumusunod na cell kung pinapatakbo mo ang halimbawang ito sa isang notebook gamit ang IPython kernel.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "1. Define the problem {#1-define-the-problem-1}"
msgstr "1. Tukuyin ang problema {#1-define-the-problem-1}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Define a random graph partitioning problem by generating a graph with randomly weighted nodes.\n"
msgstr "Tukuyin ang isang random na graph partitioning problem sa pamamagitan ng paglikha ng graph na may mga node na may random na timbang.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/guides/q-ctrl-optimization-solver/extracted-outputs/c2ce65e3-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/guides/q-ctrl-optimization-solver/extracted-outputs/c2ce65e3-0.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A standard optimization model for weighted graph partitioning can be formulated as follows. Split the nodes of the graph into three groups $g \\in \\{0, 1, 2\\}$, and let $n_{i,g} = 1$ if node $i$ is assigned to group $g$, and $n_{i,g} = 0$ otherwise. The goal is to minimize the total weight of edges whose endpoints are assigned to the same group, where the weight of an edge $(i,j)$ is the combined weight of its two endpoints, $\\omega_{i,j} = \\omega_i + \\omega_j$:\n"
msgstr "Ang isang standard optimization model para sa weighted graph partitioning ay maaaring i-formulate gaya ng sumusunod. Hatiin ang mga node ng graph sa tatlong grupo $g \\in \\{0, 1, 2\\}$, at hayaang $n_{i,g} = 1$ kung ang node $i$ ay itinalaga sa grupo $g$, at $n_{i,g} = 0$ kung hindi. Ang layunin ay i-minimize ang kabuuang timbang ng mga edge kung saan ang mga endpoint ay itinalaga sa parehong grupo, kung saan ang timbang ng isang edge $(i,j)$ ay ang pinagsamang timbang ng dalawa nitong endpoint, $\\omega_{i,j} = \\omega_i + \\omega_j$:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "$$\\textbf{Minimize}\\qquad y = \\sum_{(i,j)\\in E} \\omega_{i,j} \\sum_{g} n_{i,g}\\, n_{j,g}$$\n"
msgstr "$$\\textbf{Minimize}\\qquad y = \\sum_{(i,j)\\in E} \\omega_{i,j} \\sum_{g} n_{i,g}\\, n_{j,g}$$\n"

# doq: fixed after review 2026-09-29
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Every node must be assigned to exactly one of the three groups. This is a Hamming-weight-1 constraint: for every node $i$, exactly one of $n_{i,0}, n_{i,1}, n_{i,2}$ must equal 1, and the rest must equal 0:\n"
msgstr "Dapat maitalaga ang bawat node sa eksaktong isa sa tatlong grupo. Ito ay isang Hamming-weight-1 constraint: para sa bawat node $i$, eksaktong isa sa $n_{i,0}, n_{i,1}, n_{i,2}$ ang dapat maging 1, at ang natitira ay dapat maging 0:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "$$n_{i,0} + n_{i,1} + n_{i,2} = 1 \\texttt{ for all } i \\in V$$\n"
msgstr "$$n_{i,0} + n_{i,1} + n_{i,2} = 1 \\texttt{ for all } i \\in V$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Rather than encoding this requirement as a penalty term in the cost function, pass it directly to the Solver as a hard constraint using the `constraint` input.\n"
msgstr "Sa halip na i-encode ang requirement na ito bilang isang penalty term sa cost function, ipasa ito nang direkta sa Solver bilang isang hard constraint gamit ang `constraint` input.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\" title=\"Partially constrained problems\">\n"
"You do not need to add every variable to `constraint`. Any variable left out of the dictionary remains unconstrained, so you can mix hard-constrained groups of variables with free variables in the same problem.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\" title=\"Mga bahagyang constrained na problema\">\n"
"Hindi mo kailangang idagdag ang bawat variable sa `constraint`. Ang anumang variable na hindi kasama sa dictionary ay mananatiling unconstrained, kaya maaari mong pagsamahin ang mga hard-constrained na grupo ng mga variable kasama ang mga malayang variable sa parehong problema.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "2. Run the problem {#2-run-the-problem-1}"
msgstr "2. Patakbuhin ang problema {#2-run-the-problem-1}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Calculate the function size using the binary decision variables and interactions from the objective function and constraints. This formulation uses one variable per node and group. Pass the calculated size to `solver.run` through `function_size`.\n"
msgstr "Kalkulahin ang function size gamit ang mga binary decision variable at interaksyon mula sa objective function at mga constraint. Gumagamit ang formulation na ito ng isang variable kada node at group. Ipasa ang nakalkulang laki sa `solver.run` sa pamamagitan ng `function_size`.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "3. Get the result {#3-get-the-result}"
msgstr "3. Kunin ang resulta {#3-get-the-result}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Retrieve the solution and analyze the results. The solution cost represents the total weight of edges whose endpoints ended up in the same group, so a lower cost indicates a better partitioning of the graph.\n"
msgstr "Kunin ang solusyon at suriin ang mga resulta. Ang cost ng solusyon ay kumakatawan sa kabuuang timbang ng mga edge kung saan ang mga endpoint ay napunta sa parehong grupo, kaya ang mas mababang cost ay nagpapahiwatig ng mas mahusay na partitioning ng graph.\n"

